  <data name="HelpText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Click a picture to put it on the desktop. It changes at once, so you can see it where it will be.

Add copies pictures into your own wallpaper folder, so moving or deleting the original later does not take the desktop with it. Pictures can also be dropped on the list from the desktop or a Files window. Remove deletes one of your own copies; the pictures that come with wlRIX cannot be removed.

Fit says how a picture meets the screen. Color is what shows around it, through anything transparent in it, and on its own under No Picture.

Desk chooses which background you are changing. All Desks is the one every desk shows unless it has its own; choosing a desk changes that desk's own background, which it shows while it is the desk on screen. Use Shared Background takes a desk's own background away again.

With "Use on the lock screen too" checked, the lock screen shows the same background as All Desks.

Reset puts back what the desktop had when this window opened. Cancel does the same and then closes; OK keeps what you chose.</value>
